    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Set on an exceptional 3.6-acre site of which c.1 acre is of formal gardens and the remaining 2.6 acres is under wild, natural land just a short stroll from Oysterbed Pier, this superb detached residence offers a rare combination of coastal lifestyle, generous living accommodation and complete privacy in a truly idyllic setting.\r\n\r\nDesigned with both comfort and character in mind, the home of c.203 sq mtrs features three spacious double bedrooms, two of which benefit from beautifully appointed ensuite bathrooms and walk-in wardrobes. A family bathroom serves the remaining accommodation.\r\n\r\nAt the heart of the home is a stunning open-plan kitchen, dining and living space with full-height ceilings and striking exposed beams, creating a wonderful sense of light and space throughout. Ideal for both everyday family living and entertaining, this impressive room forms the centrepiece of the property. A second cosy sitting room provides the perfect retreat for quieter evenings.\r\n\r\nFurther accommodation includes a practical utility room with rear access and a large office room which could easily be used as a fourth bedroom, while outside the property continues to impress with a separate detached garage and expansive grounds extending to approximately 3.6 acres of easy to maintain gardens.\r\n\r\nAdding further appeal, the property is being offered fully furnished which has been done to a very high standard and inclusive of all contents, including a large boat, kayaks, gardening equipment and tools — presenting an outstanding turnkey opportunity for purchasers seeking either a permanent residence, holiday retreat or lifestyle investment.\r\n\r\nSome further features of this beautiful property included the following, the house is fitted with a new HVAC system as ancillary heating, this continually cleans and warms the air 24/7.\r\n\r\nHeating in bathrooms is electric underfloor.\r\n\r\nHeating in all rooms is by infra-red panels in the ceilings and each room has individual temperature control, meaning no boiler repairs or oil storage tank.\r\n\r\nThe house was manufactured in Canada by Normerica to a very high Canadian standard using a post and beam construction and the wall panels and roof panels are SIPS ( structural insulated panels) which are thermally efficient.\r\n\r\nNo expense was spared in either the construction or fixtures and fittings.\r\n\r\nBathrooms are fitted with Perrin & Rowe taps.\r\n\r\nWith its peaceful coastal setting, generous proportions and unique inclusions, this is a truly special property offering an enviable lifestyle close to the water and surrounded by natural beauty."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Accommodation Details – Dimensions as per floor plan\r\n\r\nOpen plan Kitchen/dining/living room: tiled floor, fitted kitchen units, electric hob & oven. Full ceiling height with exposed beams. Solid fuel stove in main living area.\r\n\r\nSitting room: Wooden floor, solid fuel stove.\r\n\r\nBedroom 1: wooden floor, built in closet\r\nEn-suite: fully tiled, shower, wc & whb\r\n\r\nBedroom 2: wood floor, walk in closet\r\nEn-suite: tiled floor, half tiled wall, bath, shower, wc & whb\r\n\r\nUtility: tiled floor, storage units, sink, rear door access\r\n\r\nMain Bathroom: tiled floor, partially tiled wall, shower, wc & whb\r\nBedroom 3: twin room, wood floor, closet.\r\n\r\nBedroom 4/Office: wood floor"
      },
